### Test /analysis endpoint (unknown field, Because StrictModel forbids extras, this should fail validation.)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/analyse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "My order is late.",
  "force_priority": "urgent"
}


### Test /generate-response endpoint
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "My order was due yesterday and I am frustrated because it still has not arrived."
}


### Test /generate-response endpoint (use ORD-1005 because it is scoped to CUST-104.)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "Where is my order? It is late.",
  "customer_id": "CUST-104",
  "order_id": "ORD-1005"
}


### Test /generate-response endpoint (Wrong-customer request — this must not expose the order as trusted context.)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "Where is my order?",
  "customer_id": "CUST-101",
  "order_id": "ORD-1005"
}


### Test /generate-response endpoint (Order without customer — request validation should reject this before database or Claude work)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/generate-response
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_message": "Where is my order?",
  "order_id": "ORD-1005"
}


### Test /tickets endpoint (This request should analyse the message, create application metadata, and persist the result)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "CUST-104",
  "order_id": "ORD-1005",
  "message": "My order is late again. Where is it?"
}


### Test /tickets endpoint (retrieve above ticket)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/tickets/TKT-8edb72f8

### Test /tickets endpoint (list customer tickets)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/tickets?customer_id=CUST-104


